# AMD64 thunk export spec -- secur32.dll.
#
# SSPI.  Cyberpunk 2077's REDGalaxy64.dll LoadLibrary()s this for its TLS
# to GOG's services, and a guest namespace without it is the fatal shape:
# the loader finds the native ppc64 builtin, correctly refuses to splice it
# into a guest call, the LoadLibrary fails, and REDGalaxy throws
# gog::RuntimeError (measured: the e06d7363 throw-info in REDGalaxy64.dll
# names .?AVRuntimeError@gog@@), which the engine treats as fatal init --
# REDEngineErrorReporter and exit 3 before d3d12 ever loads.  The emulated
# lane loads wintrust and this module at the same point and boots.
#
# InitSecurityInterfaceW is GUEST-IMPL, and this is load-bearing: the real
# export returns a SecurityFunctionTable full of NATIVE function pointers,
# and a guest calling through one of those is the native-pc-in-a-guest-image
# failure class.  REDGalaxy64 GetProcAddress()es exactly this name and throws
# gog::RuntimeError on NULL, so the absent export was not survivable either.
# __wine_guest_InitSecurityInterfaceW (ntdll, forwarded through this module's
# .spec) builds the table from the GUEST thunk module's own stub addresses.
# The A variant stays EXCLUDED until a title proves it needs the same.
#
# sspi.h carries the whole SSPI surface and nothing in the oracle's default
# translation unit includes it; without it 52 of 61 exports were refused as
# "no declaration found" and only the Lsa* nine emitted.
DLL secur32.dll
FROM-SPEC auto
PROBE-EXTRA sspi.h
EXCLUDE   InitSecurityInterfaceA
GUEST-IMPL   InitSecurityInterfaceW   __wine_guest_InitSecurityInterfaceW
